<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Did we in our own strength confide,</l><l>Our striving would be losing;</l><l>Were not the right Man on our side,</l><l>The Man of God’s own choosing:</l><l>Dost ask who that may be?</l><l>Christ Jesus, it is He;</l><l>Lord Sabaoth His Name,</l><l>From age to age the same,</l><l>And He must win the battle.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>And though this world, with devils filled,</l><l>Should threaten to undo us,</l><l>We will not fear, for God hath willed</l><l>His truth to triumph through us:</l><l>The Prince of Darkness grim,</l><l>We tremble not for him;</l><l>His rage we can endure,</l><l>For lo! his doom is sure,</l><l>One little word shall fell him.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>That word above all earthly powers,</l><l>No thanks to them, abideth;</l><l>The Spirit and the gifts are ours</l><l>Through Him who with us sideth:</l><l>Let goods and kindred go,</l><l>This mortal life also;</l><l>The body they may kill:</l><l>God’s truth abideth still,</l><l>His Kingdom is forever.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
